      en: "Tralee is the county town of County Kerry in southwest Ireland, situated at the mouth of the River Lee. The town was founded in the 13th century by the Anglo-Normans and was historically a significant stronghold for the Earls of Desmond. Tralee is today a major administrative and tourism hub, known for its cultural institutions and annual events.",
