      en: ["Highest peak in Ireland at 1,038 meters", "Part of the MacGillycuddy's Reeks mountain range", "Five-meter steel summit cross was erected in 1954", "Geology consists mainly of Old Red Sandstone", "The most popular ascent is via the 'Devil's Ladder'", "Located on the Iveragh Peninsula in County Kerry"],
