      en: "Achill Island in County Mayo is the largest island off the coast of Ireland, covering 148 square kilometers. It has been connected to the mainland by the Michael Davitt Bridge since 1887. The island is defined by dramatic landscapes, including the Croaghaun Cliffs, which are among the highest in Europe, and secluded spots like Keem Bay. The Deserted Village at Slievemore provides a haunting look into the island's past.",
